// bubbler profile: spotify
//
// `mpris name="spotify"` is the exact name, not a prefix: the app's own
// id is com.spotify.Client but the player name it publishes is
// org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.spotify, which is why flathub has to name it
// explicitly too. A `*` here would own every player on the bus.
//
// The tray icon is libayatana-appindicator, which registers with
// StatusNotifierWatcher — `tray` is one rule and the item itself is
// served on the app's own unique name, so nothing needs `own`.
//
// No `talk "org.freedesktop.secrets"`, which firejail's profile grants:
// a music player's session token is adequately kept in its own config
// file in the private home, and the rule would let it talk to whatever
// process holds every password you have.
//
// `org.gnome.SettingsDaemon.MediaKeys` is GNOME's media-key grab, which
// the client asks for by that name; on any other desktop nothing owns it
// and the rule is inert. `org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver` is CEF's
// power-save blocker, which also tries `org.freedesktop.PowerManagement`
// — both names are in /opt/spotify/libcef.so, so add the second if the
// screen blanks during playback.
//
// No `portals`: Spotify has no file chooser to speak of. Add it, with
// `home-share "Music"`, if you use local files.
//
// `network` is the sandbox's own network namespace, so Spotify Connect
// finds no devices: discovery is mDNS on the LAN and pasta does not
// bridge. `network "host"` restores it at the price of the host's own
// loopback services.
wayland
dri
pipewire
network
dbus {
    talk "org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver"
    talk "org.gnome.SettingsDaemon.MediaKeys"
}
notify
tray
mpris name="spotify"
command "spotify"
